  "sourceFitAssessment": {
    "learnerTask": "Distinguish an added CAR from retained native NK activating/inhibitory inputs",
    "gap": "Converging arrows teach integration but not cell-surface contacts",
    "accuracyGuardrails": "HLA loss not guaranteed killing; no NK/T safety ranking; exact construct matters",
    "baselinePageSHA256": "d210bbab3631e5224c17bac8a72b9d1c4bdf8ecdd1307d2f815d6c0d151415db",
    "currentVisualFit": "adequate",
    "humanReview": "pending",
    "reasoning": "The membrane-to-membrane view preserves three simultaneous generic contacts: the added CAR, native activating input and native inhibitory input. The separate whole-cell response panel requires state/environment, function and harms to be assessed. Retained NK missing-self artwork supplies the original input contrast, while this extension supplies the additional CAR contact without changing ownership. HLA loss is explicitly not guaranteed killing, and there is no NK-versus-T safety ranking or receptor engineering specification."
  },
